# Keep the build context (and therefore the image) to what app/main.py actually needs at
# runtime: the app code, requirements-serving.txt, and the one model weight baked into the
# Dockerfile below. Everything else here is training data, Kaggle notebooks, other phases'
# eval artifacts, or local dev cruft that has no business being inside the serving image.
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.idea
.pytest_cache

data/
kaggle/
scripts/
Claude outputs/

# All of runs/ except the one checkpoint the Dockerfile COPYs by its exact path - Docker doesn't
# support negating a parent directory that's already excluded above with a glob, so the Dockerfile
# instead COPYs that one file explicitly rather than COPYing runs/ wholesale and trying to carve
# it back down here.
runs/

requirements.txt
requirements-serving.txt.orig
README.md
